# Feral Werewolf, the September head (ticket 45): a wide shaggy head in dark brown-grey fur with heavy cheek ruffs swept back, a mane down
# the crown and back, tall pointed ears, heavy angry brows over two amber slit eyes, an oversized pale snout with a wet black nose and the
# lower jaw hanging open, snarling with long fangs top and bottom.
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# size and the height come from the head part (content/parts/werewolf_head.sdf): normalized to the common size, the chin 4 cm lower than
# phase 1's (at 1.525 m, over the neck's top at 1.569 whose stub is inside it). The head turns on the Head bone, 0.25 m under the origin.
# The eyes are the small eye part monster_eye_amber, meshed once, used twice.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in the registry), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.614
    Part part=werewolf_head
